<section>
  <div class="num-sec">IX · What memory retains</div>
  <h2>The scale of generations</h2>
  <p class="chapo">Each generation doubles the theoretical number of ancestors: 2
  parents, 4 grandparents, 8 great-grandparents. By the sixteenth, it would take
  65,536. The chart sets what theory demands against what the registers have
  actually delivered. That collapse is the very subject of genealogy itself.</p>
