  <p style="margin-top:30px">Up to the fourth generation, memory holds: fourteen
  great-great-grandparents out of sixteen. Then the parish registers take over and
  the yield collapses — 27% at the seventh generation, 3% at the eleventh. The
  absolute maximum is reached at the eleventh generation, with fifty-nine
  identified ancestors: that is the practical limit of the Loire-Atlantique
  registers, the oldest of which go back to the mid-sixteenth century.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="num-sec">X · Living and dying</div>
  <h2>A life expectancy that declines<br>before it leaps</h2>
  <p class="chapo">Average age at death, calculated on the 1,158 people in the
  tree for whom both birth and death are known, grouped by half-century of birth.</p>
